sentences.text:
(1) The appeal filed by the Insurance Company in MFA No.32055/2013, is dismissed and the Appeal filed by the claimant in MFA No.201946/2014,
is partly allowed;
 (2) The judgment and award dated 20.05.2013  passed by the Prl. Senior Civil Judge &
 MACT, Gulbarga in MVC No.786/2012, is  modified;
 (3) The claimant is entitled to total compensation in a sum of Rs.3,58,000=00 as against a sum of Rs.2,73,600/- awarded by the Tribunal;
Umme Kausar S/O Maheboob Aalam Khazi vs Abdul Razak S/O Rukmuddin And Anr on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/35282691/
8 (4) The claimant is entitled to interest @ 6% per annum from the date of petition till its realisation;
(5) The Insurance Company shall deposit the total compensation within six weeks from the date of receipt of the copy of the order along with interest before the jurisdictional Tribunal;
(6) The amount in deposit before this court, if any, be transmitted to the jurisdictional Tribunal along with original records; (7) All other terms and conditions stipulated by the Tribunal is retained;
SD/-
